nslate these C sources:\n1. `$W/c_src/libsodium/include/sodium/private/ed25519_ref10_fe_25_5.h` (all the `static inline` fe25519 functions — the fe_25_5 representation is the one used because HAVE_TI_MODE is undefined)\n2. `$W/c_src/libsodium/crypto_core/ed25519/ref10/fe_25_5/fe.h` (fe25519_frombytes, fe25519_reduce, fe25519_tobytes)\n3. `$W/c_src/libsodium/crypto_core/ed25519/ref10/ed25519_ref10.c` **lines 1 through 262 only** (load_3, load_4, fe25519_sqmul, fe25519_invert, fe25519_pow22523, fe25519_cneg, fe25519_abs, fe25519_unchecked_sqrt, fe25519_sqrt, fe25519_notsquare). Do NOT translate anything past line 262.\n\nThis module is the SHARED field-arithmetic module that many other Rust modules will\n`use crate::ed25519_ref10_fe::*;`. Therefore:\n\n* Every function must be `#[inline]`-able `pub unsafe fn` (or `pub fn` where no raw\n  pointers are involved) with EXACTLY these names and signatures (use\n  `crate::types::fe25519`, which is `[i32; 10]`):\n\n```rust\npub unsafe fn load_3(inp: *const u8) -> u64;\npub unsafe fn load_4(inp: *const u8) -> u64;\npub fn fe25519_0(h: &mut fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_1(h: &mut fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_add(h: &mut fe25519, f: &fe25519, g: &fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_sub(h: &mut fe25519, f: &fe25519, g: &fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_neg(h: &mut fe25519, f: &fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_cmov(f: &mut fe25519, g: &fe25519, b: u32);\npub fn fe25519_cswap(f: &mut fe25519, g: &mut fe25519, b: u32);\npub fn fe25519_copy(h: &mut fe25519, f: &fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_isnegative(f: &fe25519) -> core::ffi::c_int;\npub fn fe25519_iszero(f: &fe25519) -> core::ffi::c_int;\npub fn fe25519_mul(h: &mut fe25519, f: &fe25519, g: &fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_mul32(h: &mut fe25519, f: &fe25519, n: u32);\npub fn fe25519_sq(h: &mut fe25519, f: &fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_sq2(h: &mut fe25519, f: &fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_reduce(h: &mut fe25519, f: &fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_pow22523(out: &mut fe25519, z: &fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_cneg(h: &mut fe25519, b: u32);\npub fn fe25519_abs(h: &mut fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_unchecked_sqrt(x: &mut fe25519, x2: &fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_sqrt(x: &mut fe25519, x2: &fe25519) -> core::ffi::c_int;\npub fn fe25519_notsquare(x: &fe25519) -> core::ffi::c_int;\npub fn fe25519_sqmul(s: &mut fe25519, n: core::ffi::c_int, a: &fe25519);\n```\n  IMPORTANT: these take `&mut`/`&` so that `fe25519_mul(&mut h, &f, &g)` works even\n  when the caller wants aliasing like `fe25519_mul(&mut t, &t.clone(), &g)`. Because C\n  allows `fe25519_mul(h, h, g)` (h aliases f), you MUST make each function copy its\n  inputs into locals FIRST (the C code already reads all of f/g into locals `f0..f9`,\n  `g0..g9` before writing h — preserve that), and ALSO provide raw-pointer-free\n  behaviour. To let callers alias, additionally provide these convenience wrappers:\n\n```rust\n// in-place-safe variants used when the caller needs h and f to be the same variable\npub fn fe25519_mul_ip(h: &mut fe25519, g: &fe25519);   // h = h * g\npub fn fe25519_sq_ip(h: &mut fe25519);                 // h = h^2\n```\n  (implement them by copying `*h` into a local and calling the main function).\n\n* Also export the three PUBLIC C symbols from `ed25519_ref10.c`/`fe.h` that appear in\n  the shared library. Check `grep -A1 'ed25519_ref10.c' $W/_cbuild/persym.txt`; they are\n  `_sodium_fe25519_frombytes`, `_sodium_fe25519_tobytes`, `_sodium_fe25519_invert`.\n  Write them as:\n\n```rust\n#[no_mangle]\npub unsafe extern \"C\" fn _sodium_fe25519_frombytes(h: *mut i32, s: *const u8) { ... }\n#[no_mangle]\npub unsafe extern \"C\" fn _sodium_fe25519_tobytes(s: *mut u8, h: *const i32) { ... }\n#[no_mangle]\npub unsafe extern \"C\" fn _sodium_fe25519_invert(out: *mut i32, z: *const i32) { ... }\n```\n  and ALSO provide safe Rust wrappers for internal use:\n```rust\npub unsafe fn fe25519_frombytes(h: &mut fe25519, s: *const u8);\npub unsafe fn fe25519_tobytes(s: *mut u8, h: &fe25519);\npub fn fe25519_invert(out: &mut fe25519, z: &fe25519);\n```\n  (the `#[no_mangle]` extern versions just forward to these).\n\nConstants (`fe25519_sqrtm1`, `ed25519_sqrtam2`, `ed25519_d`, `ed25519_d2`, `ed25519_A`,\n`ed25519_sqrtadm1`, `ed25519_invsqrtamd`, `ed25519_onemsqd`, `ed25519_sqdmone`,\n`ed25519_A_32`) ALREADY EXIST in `$W/translation/src/ed25519_ref10_tables.rs`; import\nthem with `use crate::ed25519_ref10_tables::*;`. Do not redefine them.\n\nCRITICAL correctness notes:\n* All the carry chains use `int64_t` intermediates and `(int64_t) 1 << 25` style\n  rounding; transcribe them literally with `i64` and shifts. C right-shift of a\n  negative `int64_t` is an arithmetic shift — Rust `>>` on `i64` is too. Good.\n* `fe25519_mul` uses `int32_t` truncating assignments like `h0 = (int32_t) carry...`;\n  mirror with `as i32`.\n* Use `.wrapping_add`/`.wrapping_mul` for i64/i32 arithmetic so no overflow panics.\n* Run `$W/tools/cpp.sh $W/c_src/libsodium/crypto_core/ed25519/ref10/ed25519_ref10.c`\n  if you need to see resolved macros.\n\nVerify with: `cd $W/translation && cargo build --release --target-dir $W/_chk/fe 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(error|warning: unused)\" | head -50`.\nThere must be ZERO errors attributed to `src/ed25519_ref10_fe.rs`. Ignore errors in other files.\n\nReport: the list of `pub fn`s you exported and the build status.","outputFile":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-6TMnat/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-tUprtH/3f891fde-b339-4353-9d37-1cfde3da52f8/tasks/ab03f113b02704276.output","canReadOutputFile":true}}
