pass: u32,\n    pub memory_blocks: u32,\n    pub segment_length: u32,\n    pub lane_length: u32,\n    pub lanes: u32,\n    pub threads: u32,\n    pub type_: argon2_type,\n    pub print_internals: c_int,\n}\n```\n\nNotes on implementation choices:\n- `block { v: [u64; 128] }` and `block_region { base: *mut c_void, memory: *mut block, size: usize }` defined field-for-field per `argon2-core.h`.\n- Memory allocation uses plain `malloc`/`free` from `crate::csys` (not `sodium_malloc`/mmap) — confirmed via `cpp.sh` that `argon2-core.c`'s `allocate_memory`/`argon2_verify`/`argon2_hash` all call libc `malloc`/`free` directly.\n- Single-threaded path confirmed (`ARGON2_NO_THREADS`/no pthread): `_sodium_argon2_fill_memory_blocks` iterates lanes/slices directly without any thread spawning.\n- `fill_segment` dispatch reproduced as `static mut FILL_SEGMENT: fill_segment_fn`, matching the pattern already used in `blake2b.rs` (`BLAKE2B_COMPRESS`).\n- The `G`/`BLAKE2_ROUND_NOMSG` blamka macros were transcribed as `fblamka`/`g`/`blake2_round_nomsg` helper functions using `wrapping_add`/`wrapping_mul`/`rotr64`, verified index-for-index against the fully macro-expanded `cpp.sh` output of `fill_block`/`fill_block_with_xor`.\n- Cross-module externs declared locally with `#[link_name]` for `_sodium_blake2b_long`, `_sodium_argon2_encode_string`, `_sodium_argon2_decode_string`, plus plain-named externs for `crypto_generichash_blake2b_{init,update,final}`, `sodium_memzero`, `sodium_memcmp`, `randombytes_buf` (none of these are renamed by `quirks.h`).\n- Several `argon2_validate_inputs` bound checks that are always-false given `u32`-typed fields (e.g. `outlen > 0xFFFFFFFF`) were kept literally for fidelity even though dead, matching rule 6 of the conventions.","usage":{"total_tokens":191658,"tool_uses":38,"duration_ms":701046},"uuid":"44dd437c-3b37-49e3-9d3b-e17c800d9819","session_id":"3f891fde-b339-4353-9d37-1cfde3da52f8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_inaikbqsvj2b4ywl7m7bg3b3rmrdtdg43eoh3gpgsemjgn7lj7zq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01ASjXEDWjramLtrxssYqKth","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Debug and fix mlkem768 translation","subagent_type":"general-purpose","run_in_background":true,"model":"sonnet","prompt":"You are fixing a C→Rust translation bug. Let `$W = /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-tUprtH`.\nRead `$W/CONVENTIONS.md` first.\n\nCONTEXT: `$W/translation/src/kem_mlkem768_ref.rs` is a Rust translation of\n`$W/c_src/libsodium/crypto_kem/mlkem768/ref/kem_mlkem768_ref.c`. Everything else in the\ncrate already produces byte-identical output vs. the C library, but ML-KEM-768 does NOT.\n\nEvidence (differential test, deterministic 64-byte seed `k64[i] = i*3+5`):\n```\ncrypto_kem_mlkem768_seed_keypair(pk, sk, k64) returns 0 in both, but:\n  C  first 64 bytes of pk: ef335d67243c69fc4a6a555f89b00f05f2777d593997cc2dacd0908da5196a52\n                           57c26a53235776472431b47207ae2b9b55312d2f690aae3a1541b40e0b9350a2\n  RS first 64 bytes of pk: 00576c9ff9a35db5ca01916829310e7a6c807c445fb70b26a5dba37acb2c22f4\n                           5651db306b171044859c50e77af431741c054897575af6dbbf51ca2823081e10\n```\nSo the divergence is already inside `indcpa_keypair`/`seed_keypair`. Note that\nSHA3-256/512 and SHAKE-128/256 (which this module calls through `crypto_hash_sha3*` /\n`crypto_xof_shake*`) are ALREADY VERIFIED byte-identical, so the bug is in the\npolynomial / NTT / packing / noise-sampling code, not the hashing.\n\nYOUR TASK: find and fix the bug(s) so that ML-KEM-768 matches the C exactly.\nYou may ONLY permanently modify `$W/translation/src/kem_mlkem768_ref.rs`.\n\nRECOMMENDED METHOD (do this — do not just eyeball the code):\n1. Make a scratch copy of the C file where the `static` internals are visible:\n   `mkdir -p $W/_mlkdbg && sed 's/^static //' $W/c_src/libsodium/crypto_kem/mlkem768/ref/kem_mlkem768_ref.c > $W/_mlkdbg/mlk.c`\n   (careful: only strip a leading `static ` on definitions; `static const` tables can stay\n   static — adjust the sed as needed, or simply write a C harness that `#include`s the\n   original `.c` file so all statics are in scope. The `#include` approach is cleaner:\n   ```c\n   #include \"kem_mlkem768_ref.c\"   /* gives access to every static */\n   int main(void) { ... print intermediates ... }\n   ```\n   compile with:\n   `gcc -O1 -std=c99 -w -I$W/c_src/libsodium/include -I$W/c_src/libsodium/include/sodium -I$W/c_src/libsodium/crypto_kem/mlkem768/ref -o $W/_mlkdbg/cdbg $W/_mlkdbg/harness.c -L$W/_cbuild -lsodium -Wl,-rpath,$W/_cbuild`\n   )\n2. TEMPORARILY add `#[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn __dbg_...` wrappers to\n   `kem_mlkem768_ref.rs` that expose the same intermediates, rebuild\n   (`cd $W/translation && cargo build --release`), and call them from a C harness linked\n   against `$W/translation/target/release/libsodium.so`.\n3. Bisect: compare, in order, `gen_matrix` output (the 3x3 `polyvec a[3]`),\n   `poly_getnoise_eta1` output for each of the 6 noise polys, `poly_ntt`,\n   `polyvec_pointwise_acc_montgomery`, `poly_tomont`, `polyvec_reduce`, `pack_pk`,\n   `pack_sk`. Print raw `int16_t` coefficients as decimals so sign errors are obvious.\n4. Fix the Rust to match. Likely culprits: C integer promotion of `int16_t` to `int`\n   before `>>` / `*`, `(int16_t)` truncating casts, `montgomery_reduce`'s\n   `(int32_t)(int16_t)(a * QINV)` chain, `barrett_reduce`'s `((int32_t) v * a + (1 << 25)) >> 26`,\n   `csubq`, the `rej_uniform` 12-bit unpacking, `cbd_eta1/eta2` bit extraction,\n   `poly_frombytes`/`poly_tobytes` nibble packing, the `zetas` table, or NTT loop bounds\n   / `zeta` index increments.\n5. **REMOVE every temporary `__dbg_*` export** when done, and verify with:\n   ```\n   cd $W/translation && cargo build --release\n   nm -D --defined-only target/release/libsodium.so | awk '{print $3}' | sort -u > /tmp/r.txt 2>/dev/null || \\\n     nm -D --defined-only target/release/libsodium.so | awk '{print $3}' | sort -u > $W/_mlkdbg/r.txt\n   comm -3 $W/_cbuild/csyms.txt $W/_mlkdbg/r.txt\n   ```\n   which must print NOTHING (no missing, no extra symbols).\n6. FINAL CHECK: run `$W/tools/rundiff.sh`. It must print `IDENTICAL`. If differences\n   remain, keep iterating until only non-mlkem differences (if any) are left — report\n   exactly what remains.\n\nYou may create scratch files under `$W/_mlkdbg/`. NEVER modify anything in `$W/c_src/`.\nDo not modify any other file in `$W/translation/src/`.\n\nReport: the exact bug(s) found, the fix, and the final `rundiff.sh` result."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1935,"cache_read_input_tokens":327010,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1935,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f891fde-b339-4353-9d37-1cfde3da52f8","uuid":"0712f666-d6d2-4609-8bee-6b5b9dc3d8aa","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:23:01.888Z"}
