{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ntxjt5tm3t6pratjiqvftp24ue2krl2smkhsmdfbgellsm6jkuwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`rundiff.sh` now reports `IDENTICAL (537 lines)` — full byte-for-byte match across the entire differential test suite, including ML-KEM-768.\n\nNo debug symbols were added (I found the bug by careful line-by-line static comparison against the C source, so no `__dbg_*` exports exist to clean up), and only `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-tUprtH/translation/src/kem_mlkem768_ref.rs` was modified.\n\n**Bug found:** In `poly_ntt` (line ~205) and `poly_invntt` (line ~238), the innermost NTT butterfly loop mistranslated C's `for (j = start; j < start + len; j++)`. The Rust code incremented the loop variable by `len` (`j = j + len;`) instead of by `1` (`j = j + 1;`). Since the loop condition is `j < start + len`, incrementing by `len` caused the loop body to execute exactly once instead of `len` times — most butterfly pairs in every NTT/inverse-NTT layer were simply never processed. This corrupted every downstream polynomial (`skpv`, `e`, `pkpv` in `indcpa_keypair`, and correspondingly all of `indcpa_enc`/`indcpa_dec`), which is why the public key differed completely from the very first bytes despite the underlying hash/XOF primitives being correct.\n\n**Fix:** Changed both occurrences of `j = j + len;` to `j = j + 1;` (the outer-loop update `start = j + len;` was already correct and did not need to change, since it correctly relies on `j` ending at `start + len` after the inner loop, which now happens by incrementing by 1 instead of jumping there in a single step).\n\n**Final check:** `cargo build --release` compiles cleanly (only pre-existing unrelated warnings about `randombytes_buf` signature mismatches across other modules, not part of this file), and `$W/tools/rundiff.sh` prints `IDENTICAL (537 lines)` with no diff — ML-KEM-768 (and everything else) now matches the C library exactly."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":191,"cache_read_input_tokens":75164,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":191,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01ASjXEDWjramLtrxssYqKth","session_id":"3f891fde-b339-4353-9d37-1cfde3da52f8","uuid":"ff2ff157-7365-41ad-b042-3e394d21eb13","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:25:09.606Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Debug and fix mlkem768 translation"}
