{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_c3iif36kqhn7cqi6kg4c5b25vwhrie2tjikfgqnerggwgzluh7ha","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The complete libsodium 1.0.23 library is translated to Rust.\n\n**Result — verified, not just compiling:**\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo build --release` (clean rebuild) | succeeds, 0 errors |\n| `nm -D` exported symbols: C `.so` vs Rust `.so` | **890 vs 890, diff empty** (no missing, no extra) |\n| Differential test phase 1 (537 lines of outputs) | **byte-identical** |\n| Differential test phase 2 (757 lines: error paths, edge cases, long inputs) | **byte-identical** |\n| `c_src/` modified | no |\n\n**Scope covered:** all 114 C files that contribute symbols (the 25 SIMD/asm variants compile to nothing under the reference `no HAVE_*` config, so their portable fallbacks are what's reproduced) → 60 Rust modules, ~27k lines, `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`, zero external dependencies (libc bound by hand since the sandbox has no crates.io access).\n\nIncludes the macro-renamed linker symbols from `private/quirks.h` (e.g. `blake2b_init` → `_sodium_blake2b_init`, `ge25519_p3_add` → `_sodium_ge25519_p3_add`, `argon2_ctx` → `_sodium_argon2_ctx`, `escrypt_r` → `_sodium_escrypt_r`) and the exported data objects (`aegis128l_soft_implementation`, `crypto_stream_chacha20_ref_implementation`, `randombytes_sysrandom_implementation`, …).\n\n**Bugs I found and fixed during verification** (both caught by the differential harness / symbol diff, not by trusting sub-agent self-reports):\n- `poly_ntt`/`poly_invntt` in ML-KEM-768: inner butterfly loop incremented by `len` instead of `1`, so most butterflies never ran — corrupted every ML-KEM and X-Wing output.\n- `ge25519_p2_dbl`: two self-aliasing `fe25519_sub` calls needed a temporary copy.\n\n**Reproduction tooling left in place:** `tools/cpp.sh` (shows the exact post-preprocessor C for any file), `tools/difftest.c`, `tools/difftest2.c`, `tools/rundiff.sh`, `CONVENTIONS.md`.\n\nOne caveat worth stating plainly: the two harnesses exercise every public primitive plus many error/edge paths, but they are not exhaustive — untested corners (unusual `sodium_misuse()` triggers, the guarded-heap paths that this build config compiles out, huge-input overflow guards) rest on line-by-line fidelity rather than measured equality."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":215,"cache_read_input_tokens":371095,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":215,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f891fde-b339-4353-9d37-1cfde3da52f8","uuid":"8acaf2a8-807e-4e77-9c3c-e34cbb39db81","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:29:12.290Z"}
